          forms: ["[N] + に{反|はん}して", "[N] + に{反|はん}し", "[N] + に{反|はん}する + [N]", "[N] + に{反|はん}した + [N]"],
          formNotes: [
            { ja: "「{予想|よそう}・{期待|きたい}・{意向|いこう}」などと一緒に使われる。", en: "Used together with nouns such as 予想 (prediction), 期待 (expectation) and 意向 (intention).", gen: true },
          ],
          examples: [
            { ja: "今回の{経済政策|けいざいせいさく}は国民の{期待|きたい}に{反|はん}して、まったく{効果|こうか}がなかった。", en: "Contrary to the public's expectations, this economic policy had no effect at all." },
            { ja: "彼は、親の{意向|いこう}に{反|はん}して、{戦場|せんじょう}カメラマンになった。", en: "Against his parents' wishes, he became a war photographer." },
            { ja: "{実験結果|じっけんけっか}は{予想|よそう}に{反|はん}するものだったので、{関係者|かんけいしゃ}はがっかりした{様子|ようす}だった。", en: "The experimental results were contrary to predictions, so the people involved looked disappointed." },
            { ja: "{手作|てづく}りにこだわってきた{店主|てんしゅ}の{意|い}に{反|はん}することだが、{人件費削減|じんけんひさくげん}のため、{機械化|きかいか}せざるを{得|え}ない{状況|じょうきょう}になってきた。", en: "It goes against the wishes of the owner, who has always insisted on handmade products, but to cut labor costs we've reached a point where we have no choice but to mechanize." },
          ],
          deepDive: "**反する** means *to go against, be contrary to*. **Nに反して** = *contrary to N*: the result or situation turned out **opposite to what was predicted or expected** (the book). N is typically a noun of expectation or intention — the ＊ note lists 予想, 期待, 意向: しかし生物学者の期待に反して、この計画はすぐには実行されなかった (*contrary to the biologists' hopes, however, the plan wasn't carried out right away*, the sample).\n\nForms (the book) — exactly what the practice tests:\n- **に反して / に反し** link to a **clause or predicate**: 予想に反して決勝戦まで進んだ (*contrary to predictions, they reached the final*). に反し is the written form.\n- **に反する + N / に反した + N** modify a **noun**: 予測に反する結果 (*a result contrary to the forecasts*), 予想に反した展開 (*an unexpected turn of events*). The noun must follow immediately.\n\nDirection: the outcome can be better **or** worse than expected. 予想に反して無名のランナーが優勝した (*an unknown runner won, against the predictions*) is a pleasant surprise; 期待に反して、まったく効果がなかった (*contrary to hopes, it had no effect at all*) a disappointment.\n\nWith wills, rules or norms, 〜に反する means *go against, violate*: 親の意向に反して戦場カメラマンになった (*he became a war photographer against his parents' wishes*), 労働者の意思に反して (*against the workers' will*), 店主の意に反する (*against the owner's wishes*), 法律に反する行為 (*an act that breaks the law*).\n\nDon't confuse it with:\n- **〜にもかかわらず** (#21), *despite ~*: its premise is a fact (雨にもかかわらず, *despite the rain*); に反して needs an expectation or will.\n- **〜に関して** (#68), *about*: 予想に関して意見を述べる (*give views about the forecast*) — no contrast.\n- **〜に対して**, *toward, in contrast to* — neutral, not about expectations.\n- **〜どおり（に）**, *as ~*: the opposite: 予想どおり (*as predicted*).\n\nCommon mistake: a noun that isn't an expectation: ✗天気に反して → ✓天気予報に反して (*contrary to the weather forecast*).\n\nJLPT tip: review 問題1-1: 大方の予想に反して、初出場の無名のランナーが優勝した (*contrary to most people's predictions, an unknown first-time runner won*). Look for 予想・期待・予測・意向・イメージ before the blank: in 問題2, パンダは外見のイメージに反して凶暴な一面がある (*contrary to the image their appearance gives, pandas have a violent side*) — に反して links to the predicate (一面がある), so the て-form is used.",
