          xref: "☞ p.220　〜{上|うえ}／{上|じょう}",
          deepDive: "**N上（じょう）** is a Sino-Japanese suffix meaning *from the standpoint of N, in terms of N* — the book: 〜の点から考えて, used with words that name a viewpoint. It turns a noun into an adverbial (理論上は可能だ, *it's possible in theory*) or, with の, a noun modifier (歴史上の人物, *a historical figure*; 健康上の理由, *health reasons*).\n\nConnection (the book): **N + 上**, directly after a (usually two-kanji) noun. The ＊ note lists typical partners: 理論・職業・教育・法律・歴史・表面. Learn the common ones as vocabulary:\n- 理論上 *in theory*, 事実上 *in effect, de facto*, 形式上 *formally*, 表面上 *on the surface*, 書類上 *on paper*\n- 法律上 *legally*, 歴史上 *historically*, 職業上 *professionally*, 教育上 *educationally*, 健康上 *health-wise*, 安全上／防犯上 *for safety / crime-prevention reasons*, 立場上 *because of one's position*, 経営上 *from a business standpoint*, 契約上 *under the contract*\n\nTypical shapes:\n- **〜上は…が／けど** — theory or appearance vs. reality: あの2人は表面上は親しそうに見えるけど、本当はあまり仲がよくない (*those two look close on the surface, but they don't really get along*); 書類上は存在するが経営実態のない会社 (*a company that exists on paper but does no actual business*).\n- **〜上の + N**: 防犯上の理由から (*for crime-prevention reasons*, review 問題2).\n- **〜上、…** as a reason: 職業上、秘密を守らなければならない (*because of my job, I have to keep secrets*).\n\nReading pitfall: it's **じょう**, not うえ. The other 上 patterns (☞ p.220) are read うえ: **V上で** (#14, *in doing ~*), **〜上で** (#117, *after ~*), **〜上は** (Plus under #18, *now that ~*), **〜上（に）** (#102, *on top of ~*). N上（じょう） attaches straight to a noun, with no の or verb before it — the easiest way to tell it apart.\n\nNot every noun works: only nouns naming a field, viewpoint or criterion. ✗先生上, ✗りんご上. It's close in meaning to **〜から見ると** (#60), but more compact and formal.\n\nJLPT tip: review 問題1-3: 立場上、寮長の私が当番をサボるわけにはいかないんです (*given my position, I, the dorm leader, can't skip my turn*). において (#6), に反して (#67) and に関して (#68) don't turn 立場 into a viewpoint or reason. In the practice, keep 理論上 (*in theory*) and 事実上 (*in practice, effectively*) apart.",
