          xref: "☞ p.223　〜に{限|かぎ}る／{限|かぎ}り",
          deepDive: "**〜に限らず** is the negative of 〜に限る (*to be limited to*): *not limited to ~* → *not only ~ (but others too)*. It **widens** the scope: the noun is one example, and the rest says the same holds more broadly — the book: 〜だけでなく、ほかにも. The second half usually has **も / でも / どんな〜でも / あらゆる〜 / 〜を通して**:\n- 夏に限らず、年間を通して節電を心がけるべきだ (*we should try to save electricity all year round, not just in summer*)\n- 電化製品に限らず、あらゆる分野で新製品の開発競争が行われている (*not only in electrical appliances but in every field, companies compete to develop new products*)\n- 同じような取り組みはアメリカに限らず、ヨーロッパでも検討されている (*similar efforts are being considered not only in America but in Europe too*, the sample)\n\nConnection (the book): **N + に限らず**. For clauses (verbs, adjectives) use 〜のみならず (#63) or 〜だけでなく.\n\nRegister: formal, but also used in speech; casual speech prefers 〜だけじゃなくて.\n\nDon't confuse it with (the practice pits these against it):\n- **〜を問わず** (#2), *regardless of*: needs a noun with a range or a pair: 年齢を問わず, 男女を問わず. ✗人間を問わず — 人間 isn't a range.\n- **〜にもかかわらず** (#21), *despite*: すぐ近くにもかかわらず1時間もかかった (*it took a whole hour even though it was really close*).\n- **〜において** (#6), *in, at* (a field): 経済において — adds no further items.\n- **〜にしたがって** (#65), *as ~ changes*.\n- **〜のみならず** (#63), *not only*: same meaning, and works with clauses too.\n\nThe 限る family (☞ p.223–224): **Nに限り** (#3), *only N*; **Nに限って〜ない** (#3), *N, of all people, would never*; **V限り** (#23), *as long as*; **Nに限って** (#86), *on just that occasion (bad luck)*; **〜に限る** (#104), *~ is best*. Note the neat pair: 会員に限り (*members only*) vs 会員に限らず (*not only members*).\n\nJLPT tip: if the second half has も or でも and adds more members to the group, に限らず is likely correct. The Check: がんに限らず、病気の治療には早期発見が大事だ (*not only with cancer but with any illness, early detection is key to treatment*).",
